# Read by BuildKit for the Dockerfile beside it, whichever directory is the build context. Patterns are relative to
# that context, which is the application root in a generated application and the repository root inside nocobase3,
# so every entry is written to match at any depth.

# Rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.pnpm-store

# Runtime configuration, secrets, and data. They are mounted into the container, never copied into the image.
**/config.yml
**/config.toml
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/storage
**/database.sqlite*

# Local tooling and test output.
.git
**/.agents
**/.claude
**/.agent-annotations
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/logs
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# The application's own build, for DIST=prebuilt. Re-included last and whole, because the rules above would otherwise
# strip dependency directories inside it that happen to share a name with them, such as langchain's `storage/`.
!dist
!dist/**
!packages/templates/*/dist
!packages/templates/*/dist/**

# Except the server settings `pnpm build` extracts from local .env files, which can include DB_PASSWORD.
dist/.env
packages/templates/*/dist/.env
